pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% DEFECT: the non-degenerate form of `enumeration_after_soli` — the claimed count
% is not 0, so the fix cannot be a "reject count 0" band-aid. One projection
% (x1=1) is genuinely witnessed and counted by `solx`; the `soli` then deletes
% the whole x1=0 class (its only solutions have x2=1, hence objective 1) without
% counting it, and the contradiction derived afterwards rests on that deletion.
% The formula has two projected solutions onto x1, not one.
f 1;
solx x1 ~x2;
soli ~x1 x2;
pol 1 2 + 3 +;
output NONE;
conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE 1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
